judge_payload.judge_prompt:
You are a principal engineer evaluating the quality of a technical design document produced by an AI coding agent.

## Context
The agent was given:
1. This requirements specification:
<requirements>
"Enable brand users to create, manage, and publish campaign briefs to a creator marketplace. Core user stories: (US-1.1) Brand creates campaign with brief, budget, timeline, and creator eligibility criteria — saved as 'draft'. (US-1.2) Brand edits campaign with constraints — all fields editable in draft/pending_review, restricted edits in active (no budget change, no edits after applications received). (US-1.3) Brand submits campaign for platform review — validates required fields, budget >= min_fee, deadlines in future. (US-1.4) Admin approves or rejects with reason — notification to brand. (US-1.5) Brand pauses/resumes/cancels campaign — terminal statuses are immutable, cancel triggers creator notification. (US-1.6) Brand lists/views own campaigns with pagination and status filter. State machine: draft → pending_review → active → paused → completed → cancelled (also rejected from pending_review, with re-edit path). Key requirements: optimistic locking for concurrent edits, audit trail for status transitions, ownership authorization, deadline enforcement."
</requirements>

2. This existing system architecture context:
<system_context>
Existing FastAPI microservice 'xhs-campaign-service' (Python 3.11). Layered architecture: Model (SQLAlchemy 2.0 with Mapped[] annotations) → Repository (async, DB access only) → Service (business logic) → API (FastAPI routers under /api/v1/). PostgreSQL via asyncpg, Redis available, Celery for async tasks. Existing patterns from User module: UUID string PKs (generate_uuid()), TimestampMixin (created_at/updated_at), SoftDeleteMixin (is_deleted/deleted_at), Pydantic v2 schemas (Create/Update/Response), custom exceptions (NotFoundError, ConflictError, ForbiddenError, ValidationError), auth via X-User-Id header → CurrentUser dependency, role enforcement via require_role(). PaginatedResponse[T] generic for list endpoints. Dependency wiring: _get_service(db) factory in router module.
</system_context>

